# RFC 4517: LDAP Syntaxes and Matching Rules.
# https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4517.txt, read 2026-10-12.
#
# Every syntax of section 3.3 and every matching rule of section 4.2, copied
# mechanically from the RFC text (only the line indentation differs). The
# EXAMPLE definitions that sections 3.3.x print to illustrate a description
# syntax are not schema and are left out.
#
# Which of the rules are IMPLEMENTED, rather than merely defined, is in
# match.go. A rule defined here and not implemented makes an assertion
# Undefined (RFC 4511 4.5.1.7), which is the honest answer.

# RFC 4517, section 3.3.1 Attribute Type Description
ldapsyntax ( 1.3.6.1.4.1.1466.115.121.1.3 DESC 'Attribute Type Description' )

# RFC 4517, section 3.3.2 Bit String
ldapsyntax ( 1.3.6.1.4.1.1466.115.121.1.6 DESC 'Bit String' )

